LICENSE is the upstream ISC license. UNICODE-LICENSE covers the Unicode tables.
notice.inc preserves both notices in the host's :xu:/__ui_licenses record,
including single-executable applications. It is regenerated with the adapter.
character_data.h is upstream make gen/character.h output with canonical LF text.
character.inc is a C++17 adapter of the stateful character-break algorithm:
  - only the character_break prefix is retained; other library APIs are omitted;
  - five C99 designated arrays become constexpr std::array initializers;
  - a byte-to-enum assignment has an explicit cast;
  - the entry point is internal/static inline; likely uses a namespaced macro;
  - unused C includes and trailing whitespace are removed.
The state transitions and table expressions are unchanged. The UI wrapper
retains state across the entire string, including RI and Indic conjunct rules.

To reproduce, unpack the pinned archive, run make gen/character.h in it, then
run python3 regenerate.py PATH_TO_UNPACKED_ARCHIVE. No generator, network,
Unicode data download, or additional library is needed when building Xu apps.
